course: dictionary
lesson: 1857
title: The living fossil
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A fossil is the hard remains or print of an animal that lived long ago. Most fossils belong to animals that have died out, so no living ones are left. The coelacanth was once thought to be one of these. «The coelacanth was thought extinct for 66 million years.» Extinct means died out, so scientists believed it had disappeared along with the dinosaurs.
explain: Then, in 1938, a living coelacanth was caught off South Africa. «One was caught off South Africa in 1938.» That is why it is called a living fossil: it looked like its old relatives from millions of years ago, but it was still alive.
explain: The coelacanth lives deep down in the sea. Its fins are thick and fleshy, and they move like legs. Scientists use this clue to learn how fish are related to the animals that later walked on land.
fact: A coelacanth is a large, rare, deep-sea fish with thick fleshy fins.
fact: A «living fossil» is an animal that is still alive today but looks much like animals from millions of years ago.
fact: «Extinct» means died out, so that no living ones are left.
fact: Animals thought extinct that turn up alive again are called Lazarus species.
fact: In 1938 a coelacanth was caught in a fishing net off South Africa.
exercise: «The coelacanth was thought extinct for 66 million years.» What does extinct mean? | *Died out | Found in a fishing net | Living in shallow water | Very big
exercise: What is a coelacanth? | A small bird with bright feathers | *A large, rare, deep-sea fish with thick fleshy fins | A tree that grows in deserts
exercise: Why is the coelacanth called a living fossil? | It lives on land and climbs trees | *It looks much like its fossil relatives from millions of years ago | It was never seen before 1938 | It is made of stone
test: «In 1938 a coelacanth was caught off South Africa.» Which country was it caught near? | Indonesia | *South Africa | Australia
test: Why were scientists surprised when a coelacanth was caught? | Because the fish could fly | *Because they thought coelacanths had died out with the dinosaurs | Because it was caught in a river near their school
exam: What are Lazarus species? | Fossils kept in museums | *Animals thought extinct that turn up alive again | Fish that only live in ponds | Plants that grow on the sea floor
